INSERT INTO `nilaideskripsifinal` (`id`, `siswa_kelas_id`, `deskripsi`) VALUES
	(1, 96, 'Ayesha, I admire how much effort you’ve put into your speaking skills. You’re no longer shy to express yourself in English, and your fluency has improved a lot. Her participation in class has increased, and her pronunciation and sentence construction are much better than they were at the start. You’re on the right track keep it up!'),
	(2, 97, 'Kenzie has made excellent progress in grammar. He now uses tenses and sentence structure more correctly and consistently in both speech and writing. He used to be quiet, but now he regularly contributes to group discussions and uses English more confidently. Wishing you all the best in your next grade!'),
	(3, 98, 'Alifa has shown a remarkable improvement in her speaking confidence. At the beginning of the semester, she was hesitant, but now she speaks clearly and participates actively in discussions. Her growth is truly impressive. Wishing you all the best in your next grade!'),
	(4, 99, 'Alma you’ve grown into a curious and brave learner. You’re not afraid to ask questions and try using new expressions in class. Your progress in speaking fluency is something to be proud of! Wishing you all the best in your next grade!'),
	(5, 100, 'Ar Rayyan has gained a lot of confidence in using English. His participation in class has increased, and his pronunciation and sentence construction are much better than they were at the start. Wishing you all the best in your next grade!'),
	(6, 101, 'Arsyila it’s been a joy watching you grow, especially in expressing your ideas clearly. your confidence has improved so much, especially when speaking in front of the class. Keep practicing your writing skills. Congratulations on moving up!'),
	(7, 102, 'Asyifa\'s ability to listen and respond in English has improved greatly. She understands audio texts more easily now and is more accurate in her responses. Your love for learning is contagious. Continue to work on your self-confidence. I’ll miss your energy—good luck ahead!'),
	(8, 103, 'Azka  your improvement in pronunciation is remarkable. It’s clear you’ve been practicing outside of class. I’ve noticed how you now speak more clearly and naturally, and that has made a huge difference in how well others understand you. All the best in your next adventure!'),
	(9, 104, 'Halumi You\'ve developed a strong sense of responsibility. I\'d encourage you to participate more during discussions. You\'ve developed into a thoughtful and caring student. Work on expressing your opinions with more confidence. I’m excited for what’s ahead for you!'),
	(10, 105, 'Keenan progress in pronunciation has been significant. A few months ago, he struggled with certain sounds, but now he speaks more fluently and clearly. Your confidence has improved so much, especially when speaking in front of the class. Keep practicing your writing skills. I’m excited for what’s ahead for you!'),
	(11, 106, 'Mazel used to be shy when it came to speaking English, but he has made great strides. He now joins conversations more confidently and uses more accurate grammar in his responses. See you thrive in your new grade! '),
	(12, 108, 'Rabbani You have become more respectful and patient this year. Work a little more on proofreading your work. Your confidence has improved so much, especially when speaking in front of the class. Keep practicing your writing skills.  Best wishes in your next journey!'),
	(13, 107, 'Rifqi’s engagement in class has improved a lot. He used to be quiet, but now he regularly contributes to group discussions and uses English more confidently. You’ve shown great improvement in behavior and responsibility. Don’t forget to keep practicing your spelling. Keep it up!'),
	(14, 109, 'Nayyara’s  speaking skills have progressed beautifully. She now speaks with more fluency and less hesitation, and she uses full sentences more often than before. Your creativity and enthusiasm light up the classroom! Continue to work on staying focused during group activities. I\'m proud of you, good luck next year!'),
	(15, 110, 'Niki You\'ve shown remarkable growth this year, especially in your reading comprehension. Keep working on managing your time better during assignments. Wishing you all the best in your next grade!'),
	(16, 111, 'Prabu’s engagement in class has improved a lot. He used to be quiet, but now he regularly contributes to group discussions and uses English more confidently. Your artistic talents have grown beautifully! Continue to focus on staying organized. Good luck and keep being creative!'),
	(17, 112, 'Raihan has made noticeable improvement in speaking fluency. He now uses full sentences with correct grammar and shows much more confidence during presentations. You’ve grown into a great leader among your peers. Let’s keep building your vocabulary. All the best in your next adventure!'),
	(18, 113, 'Runako used to be shy when it came to speaking English, but he has made great strides. He now joins conversations more confidently and uses more accurate grammar in his responses. You always bring a positive attitude! Let\'s work on deepening your critical thinking skills. Congratulations and keep shining!'),
	(19, 95, 'Salsabila’s listening skills have improved steadily. She now understands instructions more quickly and responds with more confidence. Her listening comprehension is much stronger than it was before. It’s been a enjoy watching you grow, especially in expressing your ideas clearly. Continue to develop your reading fluency. Wishing you success ahead!'),
	(20, 115, 'Zachary curiosity and effort have been impressive this year. you’ve grown into a curious and brave learner. You’re not afraid to ask questions and try using new expressions in class. Your progress in speaking fluency is something to be proud of you. Keep improving your reading stamina. Congratulations and enjoy your next grade!'),
	(21, 255, 'Adeffa shows consistent effort in improving her academic skills. She is learning to express her feelings in a more constructive way. Her ability to take responsibility for her learning and behavior has also grown significantly. She has learned how to express herself more openly and has built deeper, and more meaningful friendships. Keep reaching for your dreams!'),
	(22, 256, 'Alisha has experienced meaningful improvement this year. She has strengthened her academic habits, becoming more focused and self-directed. Emotionally, Alisha has become more confident and expressive, especially during collaborative work. She now takes her responsibilities seriously and is more proactive in contributing to class life. Alisha, your personal and academic growth has been truly rewarding to witness. Keep striving and soaring!'),
	(23, 257, 'Arman has improved significantly across several areas. His academic progress is marked by increased concentration and a stronger work ethic. Early in the year. He is responsible and always gives his best effort. We’re confident that you’ll face new challenges with courage and determination. Good luck in your next adventure!'),
	(24, 258, 'Fadhil has made significant strides in both academic and personal development. At the start of the year, he struggled with staying focused and completing tasks independently, but now he consistently shows greater self-discipline and motivation to improve. Emotionally, he has learned to recognize his feelings and express them in more constructive ways. He has also become more empathetic and cooperative with his classmates. His sense of responsibility has blossomed, and he now takes pride in being accountable. Fadhil, you\'ve grown in so many ways. Carry this progress with you as you enter middle school!'),
	(25, 259, 'Farah is an exceptional student who consistently puts in great effort and displays a love of learning. Her academic performance has been outstanding, and she’s always eager to grow. Farah is emotionally mature and handles situations with kindness and understanding. Her positive energy and good judgment make her a natural leader among her peers. She takes responsibility seriously and completes every task with excellence. Farah, your journey is just beginning. Keep pursuing your dreams and never stop learning. You’ll do amazing things! '),
	(26, 260, 'Fariz has shown noticeable improvement in both his academic work and personal growth. He is becoming more confident and engaged in his learning. Fariz is learning to express his emotions more effectively, which has helped him build stronger social connections. His friendly and respectful attitude makes him a valued member of the class. Fariz is responsible and always completes his tasks with care. We’re proud of the progress you’ve made and are excited to see what lies ahead for you. All the best, Fariz! '),
	(27, 261, 'Azzam has made solid improvements throughout this academic year. Initially, he struggled with maintaining focus and completing assignments on time, but with determination, he has become more consistent and independent. Emotionally, he is becoming more aware of his emotions and has learned to express himself in calm and respectful ways. He’s sociable and makes meaningful connections with his peers. His sense of responsibility has matured, and he now takes classroom expectations more seriously. Azzam, we are proud of your journey. Keep building on this progress!'),
	(28, 262, 'Kimora is a highly motivated student who continuously strives to do her best in everything she undertakes. She has made excellent academic progress and sets a great example for her classmates. she has learned to navigate stress and disappointment with more maturity. She has formed positive relationships with peers, displaying compassion and thoughtfulness. Kimora is responsible and takes pride in the quality of her work. Congratulations on completing this chapter, Kimora. May your next journey be even more inspiring!'),
	(29, 263, 'Kinan used to be hesitant to take risks in her learning, but now she approaches new challenges with confidence and perseverance. Her emotional maturity has grown, especially in how she responds to feedback and handles peer interactions. Socially, Kinan has become more inclusive and caring, showing a stronger sense of empathy. She now takes greater ownership of her responsibilities and shows consistent follow-through. Kinan, your hard work and self-awareness have brought you far. Never stop growing and learning! '),
	(30, 264, 'Fathir has grown tremendously this year in all areas. His academic achievements are the result of hard work and dedication. He’s also become more emotionally aware, learning to pause and reflect before reacting. Fathir has grown in his ability to cooperate with classmates and resolve conflicts calmly. He now takes his classroom duties seriously and is more organized with his assignments. Fathir, your progress this year has been a joy to witness. Keep striving and believing in yourself!'),
	(31, 265, 'Mutiara has shown excellent improvement in her learning journey. Once hesitant to ask for help or share her ideas, she now confidently participates and seeks feedback to grow. She has also matured emotionally, becoming more reflective and less reactive in stressful moments. Mutiara has built stronger relationships with her peers by becoming more open and supportive. She is much more responsible with her work and handles leadership roles with care. Mutiara, your courage to grow has been inspiring. Go forward and continue to flourish!'),
	(32, 266, 'Rania is an exceptional student who consistently puts in great effort and displays a love of learning. Her academic performance has been outstanding, and she’s always eager to grow. Rania is emotionally mature and handles situations with kindness and understanding. She takes responsibility seriously and completes every task with excellence. Rania, your journey is just beginning. Keep pursuing your dreams and never stop learning.'),
	(33, 267, 'Rafa continues to grow academically and shows great determination. He is learning to express emotions in a healthy way. Rafa has become more balanced and now reacts to stress with greater control. He has also worked hard to improve his communication with peers, leading to better collaboration and stronger friendships. Rafa is responsible and always ready to help. All the best in the exciting years ahead!'),
	(34, 268, 'Raisa is a hardworking and enthusiastic student who continues to thrive academically. Her resilience and emotional awareness help her overcome challenges and support others along the way. She is a great team member who communicates effectively and listens to others’ perspectives. Raisa is dependable and often takes on leadership roles with ease. As you move forward, Raisa, hold on to your strengths and passions. You’re ready for the exciting opportunities ahead!'),
	(35, 269, 'Rasyad has experienced encouraging growth this year. He used to be quiet and unsure in academic tasks, but now he engages more confidently and produces higher-quality work. He has become more aware of his emotions and has learned to express them calmly and clearly. Rasyad has improved his communication skills and now contributes positively to group settings. His sense of responsibility has also strengthened. He now completes tasks with minimal supervision. Rasyad, your steady improvement is something to be proud of. Keep going forward with confidence!'),
	(36, 270, 'Shyvana has demonstrated strong dedication to her studies and continues to make great academic progress. She is developing a deeper understanding of her emotions and expresses herself with increasing clarity and confidence. Shyvana is kind and respectful, often going out of her way to support her friends. She handles her responsibilities with consistency and integrity. Shyvana, you have made us so proud this year. As you move on to middle school, remember to keep nurturing your talents and kindness. Best wishes!'),
	(37, 240, 'Dhafin is a calm and reliable student who has shown noticeable improvement across most subjects this year. His friendly nature makes him well-liked by peers, and he consistently shows responsibility in group work. To continue growing, Dhafin is encouraged to build more confidence in expressing his ideas, both in class discussions and during presentations. You’ve made great progress, Dhafin! Trust in yourself and let your voice be heard!'),
	(38, 241, 'Keyla brings joyful energy to the classroom and is loved by her classmates for her cheerful spirit and kindness. Her improvement in academic performance this year has been truly remarkable, a testament to her hard work and dedication. To help her learning even more, Keyla is encouraged to find moments of calm and focus during class activities. Keep shining, Keyla! Your energy is a gift, and when balanced with focus, it will take you far!'),
	(39, 242, 'Azeera is a polite and thoughtful student who follows class rules diligently. Her storytelling ability adds a unique charm to her character. She has shown good progress in attendance and punctuality, and always tries to complete the tasks given. To continue progressing, Azeera is encouraged to develop more independence and motivation in her studies. Keep trying, Azeera! You have a gentle strength that will grow with each new challenge you face!'),
	(40, 243, 'Shanum is a talented and intelligent student who consistently excels in her academic subjects. Her leadership qualities shine in both class and extracurricular activities. She is resilient, loyal, and sets a great example for her peers. To reach even greater heights, Shanum is encouraged to work on accuracy when answering test questions. You’re truly a star, Shanum! Your talents and determination are sure to lead you to great success!'),
	(41, 244, 'Cantika is a cheerful and polite student who brightens the classroom with her melodious singing and friendly attitude. She has shown significant improvement in her academic performance and is capable of completing tasks well. To continue growing, Cantika should focus on improving her concentration during lessons. Keep singing your way through learning, Cantika! Your voice and positivity are your strengths!'),
	(42, 245, 'Felice is a highly intelligent and caring student who always brings empathy and optimism into the classroom. Her ability to focus, paired with her curiosity and strong knowledge base, make her a standout learner. Felice’s consistent motivation and joy in learning inspire those around her. Keep soaring, Felice! Your heart and mind make a powerful combination!'),
	(43, 246, 'Dastan is a thoughtful and curious student with a natural talent for analysis. His class participation has improved notably, and he approaches learning with an open and empathic mindset. To improve further, Dastan should focus on sharpening his listening skills and following instructions more attentively. Keep asking questions and exploring, Dastan! Your thoughtful nature will guide your growth!'),
	(44, 247, 'Rose brings creativity and positivity to everything she does. Her sense of humor and proactive attitude make her a joy to have in class. To unlock her full potential, Rose is encouraged to put more effort into studying and reviewing class material consistently. Your bright spirit is contagious, Rose! Stay determined, and success will follow!'),
	(45, 248, 'Hilal is a calm and optimistic student who shows great empathy toward others. He has a quiet perseverance and is beginning to show more determination in his work. With continued effort, especially when tasks become more challenging, Hilal can achieve even greater results. Stay strong and keep trying, Hilal! Your kindness and patience are true strengths!'),
	(46, 249, 'Jasmine is a hardworking and insightful student who consistently demonstrates motivation and attentiveness in class. Her thoughtful contributions and friendly demeanor make her a wonderful peer and learner. Jasmine’s dedication to her studies will serve her well in the years to come. Keep up the excellent work, Jasmine! Your perseverance and insight are truly admirable!'),
	(47, 250, 'Revaldi is a determined and collaborative student who works well with peers. He takes on tasks with a positive attitude and shows steady progress in his work. To reach his full potential, Revaldi is encouraged to stay consistent in completing his daily responsibilities without reminders. You’re on the right path, Revaldi! With continued focus, you’ll achieve great things!'),
	(48, 251, 'Radhitya is a motivated and organized student who approaches his studies with determination and a positive mindset. He is friendly, patient, and contributes positively to group activities. His consistent effort and dedication to learning are commendable. Keep striving, Radhitya! Your strong character and discipline will lead you to success!'),
	(49, 252, 'Rezki is a creative and energetic student who enjoys sports and interacting with others. He brings enthusiasm to all activities, but sometimes struggles to manage emotions and maintain concentration in class. With continued support in emotional regulation and focus, Rezki can make great strides. Stay balanced, Rezki! Your energy is a strength when guided with purpose!'),
	(50, 253, 'Shanon is an analytical and enthusiastic learner who approaches tasks with curiosity and care. She is well-organized and always attentive, making her a reliable contributor in class discussions. Her love for learning is clear and will serve her well in the future. Keep exploring, Shanon! Your enthusiasm and intellect will take you far!'),
	(51, 254, 'Vino is an enthusiastic and motivated student who brings a lively spirit to the classroom. His positive attitude toward learning is commendable. To continue progressing, Vino should work on improving his focus during lessons to fully absorb the material. Keep up the great effort, Vino! Your enthusiasm is powerful when paired with focus!'),
	(52, 75, 'Arshaka is a student who has a strong grasp of various subjects, completes assignments on time, has neat handwriting, good English skills, and strong comprehension. However, he needs to improve his conversation skills to become more confident. Keep exploring new knowledge with your great spirit, Arshaka!'),
	(53, 76, 'Afifah is a kind, polite, and very obedient student. She completes her assignments on time and understands various subjects well. However, she needs to be more confident in order to improve her English performance. Hard work, heart, and hope will take you all the way, Afifah!'),
	(54, 77, 'Atalah is an active and very friendly student. However, he needs to learn to manage his emotions and improve his social interactions, as he often has conflicts with his classmates. Never stop trying to be better. Atalah!'),
	(55, 78, 'Arka is an active student. He has good calculation speed, strong memorization skills, and quick understanding. However, he needs to improve his social skills to get more confidence. Your hard work is your strength, Arka!'),
	(56, 79, 'Baby is a student with quick understanding, strong memorization skills, mastery of all subjects, and good social interaction. However, she needs to improve her speaking skills to achieve excellence. Shine bright with knowledge and kindness, Baby!'),
	(57, 80, 'Devan is an active student with quick understanding in learning and strong memorization skills. However, he needs to learn to manage his emotions and improve his social interactions with classmates to avoid conflicts. Great attitude, great future—keep going, Devan!'),
	(58, 81, 'El Zeyma excels in physical education. However, he needs to put in extra effort to improve his understanding of other academic subjects, develop faster calculation skills, and strengthen memorization. Every day is a chance to be better, Zeyma!'),
	(59, 82, 'Gibran is a student with quick understanding and strong academic skills. However, he needs to be more confident in social intraction to improve further. Always give your best, Gibran!'),
	(60, 83, 'Jihan is a student with quick understanding and memorization skills, and she excels in Tahfidz lessons. However, she needs to build more confidence to improve her understanding in English-based learning. Believe in your potential, Jihan!'),
	(61, 84, 'Kent is a student with quick understanding, disciplined, and has good social skills. You are fantastic, Kent!'),
	(62, 85, 'Alma is a reserved student who demonstrates good social interaction with her classmates. However, attention to punctuality is necessary, as she frequently arrives late. Improving her discipline in this area will contribute positively to her overall academic progress. Great work comes from great discipline, Alma!'),
	(63, 86, 'Mikail is a student with excellent comprehension skills, strong numerical abilities, and a quick memory. To reach his full potential, it is important for him to continue developing greater self-confidence. With increased confidence, Mikail is well-positioned to achieve outstanding academic success, Believe in your dreams. You can achieve them, Mikail!'),
	(64, 87, 'Zyan is a confident student with a good understanding of academic subjects and positive social interactions with his classmates. However, attention to handwriting neatness is necessary, as he would benefit from extra effort in maintaining clarity and organization in his written work. With continued focus and dedication, You are on the right path, Zyan'),
	(65, 88, 'Naomi is a bright and active student who demonstrates quick responsiveness in learning. To further support her overall development, she is encouraged to build greater confidence in using English for communication and social interaction. With continued effort, She is well on her way to achieving well-rounded excellence. Shine bright with knowledge and kindness, Naomie!'),
	(66, 89, 'Naufal is a student who is actively progressing in his understanding of various subjects. Over the past year, he has shown significant improvement, particularly in mathematics. However, he requires additional support and focus in English-based subjects to enhance his comprehension. Keep striving and growing, Naufal!'),
	(67, 90, 'Palmeto is an active, intelligent, and quick-thinking student who grasps lessons with ease. However, he is encouraged to improve his focus and time management when completing assignments to avoid delays. He also demonstrates strong creative talents, which, when combined with discipline, will greatly support his academic and personal growth. Believe in your potential, Palmeto!'),
	(68, 91, 'Raffa is a kind student who demonstrates positive character and strong friendships with his classmeet. However, he is encouraged to improve his focus during lessons and to develop a stronger sense of independence in completing assigned tasks. With greater initiative and concentration, Raffa has the potential to grow both academically and personally. Believe in your journey, trust your efforts, and embrace the growth, Raffa!'),
	(69, 92, 'Tama is an active student with good understanding and strong focus in his studies. However, there is a need for improvement in character development to support his overall growth. With continuous guidance and self-awareness, Tama has the potential to become both academically successful and well-rounded in character. Improve your character to get good future, Tama!'),
	(70, 93, 'Alea is a kind and friendly student who has shown noticeable improvement in her understanding of the lessons. She has also demonstrated progress in maintaining focus during learning activities and has developed positive interactions with her classmeet. Her continued growth is commendable and reflects her dedication to learning. Keep your growth, Alea!'),
	(71, 94, 'Rayhan is a kind and friendly student who maintains positive social relationships with his classmeet. However, he requires additional effort in understanding the lessons. Attention should also be given to improving the neatness of his handwriting and maintaining consistent punctuality. You should be focus and more spirit everyday, Rayhan!'),
	(72, 114, 'Billa has shown significant improvement in her self-confidence, understanding of lessons, and social interaction with her peers. Her progress is commendable and reflects her growing commitment to learning and personal development. Your hard work is your strength, Billa!'),
	(73, 116, 'Abiyyah has made great progress in her studies. She is improving in managing her time wisely. She takes responsibility for her actions and shows maturity. She is also a kind and respectful student. Keep up the good work Abiyah!'),
	(74, 117, 'Nawal is becoming more confident in her abilities, and it\'s wonderful to see. She handles her tasks with great diligence and care. She shows great empathy towards others, makes learning environment welcoming. Great job, Nawal!'),
	(75, 118, 'Alesha has made great progress in her studies. She takes responsibility for learning and completes tasks with care and diligence. She follows the rules and instructions well. She is also learning to handle challenges with patience and resilience. Keep going Alesha!'),
	(76, 119, 'Alfun has made great progress in her studies. She stays focused during lessons, which helps her absorb knowledge effectively. She is dependable and trustworthy, and her classmates look up to her. Great job Alfun!'),
	(77, 120, 'Assyifa’s curiosity and eagerness to learn are truly inspiring. She takes initiative in her learning, showing strong self-motivation. Her consistency in completing her assignments on time is impressive. She is a kind and respectful student, and her classmates appreciate her support. Great job Assyifa!'),
	(78, 121, 'Azizah made a good teamwork and cooperation makes her a valuable part of the class. She is improving in managing her time wisely. She still needs to work on focus and concentration during class time. Keep pushing forward Azizah!'),
	(79, 122, 'Raisa is enthusiastic in class but needs to focus more on task completion and she is still learning to manage responsibilities more independently. She is still developing self-confidence and occasionally needs support in social situations. Keep up the good work Raisa!'),
	(80, 123, 'Bibi is a quiet but hardworking student. She has made great strides in emotional development and is showing more responsibility in completing assignments. She is still developing self-confidence and occasionally needs support in social situations. Keep up the good work, Bibi!'),
	(81, 124, 'Ezza participates actively in class and shows emotional growth, his academic progress is good. He is learning to take more responsibility in group work and independent tasks. He is respectful and kind. He is still working on becoming more disciplined with routines. Keep up the good work Ezza!'),
	(82, 125, 'Fauzan is a mature and responsible student. He demonstrates excellent emotional regulation and a strong commitment to his studies. He shows consistent progress in academic tasks and demonstrates a strong desire to learn. Good job Fauzan!'),
	(83, 126, 'Alfayed has a positive attitude toward learning. He sometimes needs reminders to stay on task, but he shows good emotional awareness and willingness to improve. He works well in groups and shows empathy toward others. Keep up the good work Alfayed!'),
	(84, 127, 'Azka has shown great progress in his learning and actively participated in discussions. He is socially thoughtful and collaborates well with peers. His discipline and sense of responsibility are commendable. Good job Azka!'),
	(85, 128, 'Najua is making steady progress academically. She is learning to regulate her emotions and shows improved discipline in daily routines. She is still developing self-confidence and occasionally needs support in social situations. Keep up your spirit Najua, you can do it!'),
	(86, 129, 'Nayyira is focused and engaged in class activities. She fosters positive relationships with peers and maintains discipline. Her sense of responsibility makes her a reliable team member. Good job Nayyira!'),
	(87, 130, 'Kara approaches learning with enthusiasm and creativity. He communicates well with others and manages conflicts effectively. His discipline and willingness to take responsibility are admirable. Keep up the good work Kara!'),
	(88, 131, 'Qaireen takes learning seriously and challenges herself intellectually. She builds meaningful connections with classmates. Her discipline and commitment to responsibilities are praiseworthy. Good job Qaireen!'),
	(89, 132, 'Radin displays consistent effort in his studies and never hesitates to help others. He is emotionally aware and fosters a positive environment. His discipline and responsibility are commendable. Continue to improve your achievements, good job Radin!'),
	(90, 133, 'Enand is enthusiastic in class but needs to focus more on task completion. He is friendly and social but still learning to manage responsibilities more independently. Keep your spirit Enand!'),
	(91, 134, 'Syakila shows consistent progress in her academic learning. She is emotionally mature and builds positive relationships with peers. Her discipline and sense of responsibility are commendable. Continue to improve your achievements Syakila!'),
	(92, 135, 'Zayn is dedicated to his studies and always seeks improvement. He has strong interpersonal skills and maintains emotional stability. His punctuality and responsible attitude reflect his discipline. Good job Zayn!'),
	(93, 219, 'Affandy demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. He started to get used to completes his assignments on time. Some of the time, Affandy shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time alone. but lately, he started to have lot of friend. Keep moving, you are improving!'),
	(94, 220, 'Aisyah demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in most of the subjects. She shows a better ability to complete her assignments on time. Most of the time, Aisyah shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Nice going!'),
	(95, 221, 'Alfa demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in some of the subjects. He shows a better ability to complete his assignments on time. Alfa  demonstrates a beginning level of behaviour with honesty and integrity at all times. He is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time alone. Recently, Alfa has also completed his sima\'an retirement. Hopefully he will continue to be remembered and istiqamah. May your life be blessed and continue to be successful in the future!'),
	(96, 222, 'Qonita demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Qonita show her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is learning to manage emotional abilities appropriately and respond well to feedback. He also chooses a good environment of friends so he can study together. I believe you can do it!'),
	(97, 223, 'Yasmine demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in some of the subjects. She always complete her assignments on time. Yasmine shows progress in behaving with honesty and integrity at all times. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time alone. You are precious and sweet!'),
	(98, 224, 'Athalla demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. He  demonstrates a developing level of responsibility and sometimes needs to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. He makes friends quickly in the classroom and chooses to spend free time with friends. he have the critical thinking tyhan others. you glow, keep the faith!'),
	(99, 225, 'Intan demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She shows a better ability to complete her assignments on time. Rarely does Intan show her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She needs to learn how to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. You are fantastic, you are on your way!'),
	(100, 226, 'Farryall demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. Rarely does Farryall show his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with close friends. please, take more focus on your job and keep learning ya!'),
	(101, 227, 'Adies demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. She shows a better ability to complete her assignments on time. Rarely does Adies show her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with friends. Gladies good at sport and phisycal subjects. She treat other friend with kindly also. good attitude will bring good things also!'),
	(102, 228, 'Janeeta demonstrates an excelent level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Janeeta show her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with friends. Just Don\'t be easily influenced by some things out there!'),
	(103, 229, 'Kenzie demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in some of the subjects. He shows a better ability to completes his assignments on time. Kenzie  demonstrates a beginning level of behaviour with honesty and integrity at all times. He is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with friends. take it slow, because you are a very careful and detailed person!'),
	(104, 230, 'Kirana demonstrates an excelent level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Kirana shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with friends. Come and let\'s balance provisions for this dunya and akhirah!'),
	(105, 231, 'Letisha demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Letisha shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time alone. take what good for you, and leave what bad for you!'),
	(106, 232, 'Mikha demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. Rarely does Mikha shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with other boys in the class. keep improving your skill!'),
	(107, 233, 'Keenan demonstrates an excelent developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. Rarely does Keenan shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with other boys in the class. keep the spirit up!'),
	(108, 234, 'Ayun demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Ayun shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time with close friends. She is very kind  and sweet to everyone. so keep shining for your parents!'),
	(109, 235, 'Raja demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. Rarely does Raja shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He is able to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Good manners and politeness are teh important thing!'),
	(110, 236, 'Shakila demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in most of the subjects. She seldom completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Shakila shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She makes friends quickly in the classroom and chooses to spend free time with friends. It takes a lifetime to make a friend, but it only takes us a day to lose all. Don\'t repeat the same mistake. You are great till today!'),
	(111, 237, 'Jihan demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Jihan shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time together with friends. you can if you want. keep trying!'),
	(112, 238, 'Stefany demonstrates a excelent developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She shows a better ability to completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Stefany shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time alone. Wow! way to go. Super, you’re special.'),
	(113, 239, 'Timori demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She shows a better ability to completes her assignments on time. She demonstrates a developing level of responsibility and sometimes needs to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. She is learning to manage emotional abilities appropriately and respond well to feedback. nothing is impossible if you try to be best!'),
	(114, 136, 'Abi shows good responsibility in completing assignments on time and demonstrates a good level of understanding, although improvement is still needed in some areas. Greater discipline in classroom behavior is encouraged to support a more effective learning process. Keep spirit, Abi!'),
	(115, 138, 'Bella has good knowledge in most subjects and is able to follow the lessons well in class. While she performs well overall, there are a few subjects that still require improvement. Additionally, she has to encourage to speak more confidently and assertively. Keep up the good work, Bella!'),
	(116, 139, 'Alfath has shown good progress in almost all subjects, with only a few areas that still need improvement. He is confident when answering questions in front of the class and working well in group discussions. However, he sometimes needs to stay more focused during lessons because he can be easily distracted by his peers. Keep up the good work, Alfath!'),
	(117, 140, 'Arkan demonstrates a good understanding of the lessons, although there is still room for improvement in certain subjects. He maintains a positive and respectful attitude in class, setting a good example for others. However, he is encouraged to be more competitive and actively engage in class activities to further enhance her performance. Keep up the good work, Arkan! '),
	(118, 141, 'Awal has a good understanding in most subjects and he has good attendances in class. He has the potential to progress even further with more consistent effort and focus. But, he simply needs to build more confidence and deepen his understanding of the material to show clearer improvement and reach his full potential. Keep spirit, Awal!'),
	(119, 142, 'Axl is still in the process of developing a better understanding of the lessons. More effort and consistent practice are needed to help strengthen him grasp the material.  He needs to improve his class attendance to ensure continuous learning and better academic progress. Setting clear goals and staying consistent will make a big difference. Keep trying, and don\'t give up, Axl!'),
	(120, 143, 'Leya has consistently demonstrated a strong understanding across all subjects and achieved excellent results. She maintains a positive and respectful attitude in class, as well as sets a great example for her peers. Her competitive spirit and drive to succeed are evidence in her active participation and consistent performance. Keep up the outstanding work, Leya!'),
	(121, 144, 'Kiyya has shown noticeable improvement in understanding several subjects. She demonstrates a positive attitude in class and is not hesitant to ask questions when facing difficulties, which reflects her willingness to learn. However, there is still room to be more competitive and actively engaged during class activities with a bit more confidence and participation, she can further enhance her overall performance. Keep up the good work, Kiyya!'),
	(122, 145, 'Hana has a good understanding in all subjects and has shown improvement in her grades this term. She demonstrates good behavior in class and is disciplined in submitting homework and completing class assignments. Her attendance is excellent. However, she is encouraged to build more self-confidence and not be afraid of making mistakes, as they are part of the learning process. Keep up the good work, Hana!'),
	(123, 146, 'Gibran demonstrates an excellent understanding of the lessons and consistently performs at a high level. He remains highly focused during class and shows strong competitive skills, he always strives to give his best. His overall performance is outstanding, and his positive attitude toward learning is truly commendable. Keep up the great work, Gibran!'),
	(124, 147, 'Kieran demonstrates a very strong and consistent understanding of the lessons. She is highly responsible and consistently submits her assignments promptly, often being the fastest in class. She is not hesitant to ask for help when facing difficulties, which reflects her willingness to learn and improve. However, she is encouraged to develop a more competitive spirit and expand her social interactions beyond her usual group of friends. Stepping out of her comfort zone will help her grow both academically and socially. Keep up the great work, Kieran!'),
	(125, 148, 'Mizan has an excellent understanding of the subjects and is not hesitant to ask questions when in doubt, which is a great quality. He maintains a positive and respectful attitude in class, as well as sets a great example for his peers. His competitive spirit and drive to succeed are evidence in his active participation and consistent performance. Keep up the good work, Mizan! '),
	(126, 149, 'Nara shows a willingness to learn but still requires additional guidance to strengthen her understanding of the lessons.  However, she is often drowsy during class, which can affect her concentration and learning. She needs to get enough rest and stays focused to make the most of her learning opportunities. With consistent support and encouragement, she will be able to understand the material more effectively and improve her overall performance slowly but surely. Keep spirit, Nara!'),
	(127, 150, 'Nezha shows good responsibility in completing assignments on time and demonstrates a satisfactory level of understanding, although improvement is still needed in some areas. Greater discipline in classroom behavior is encouraged to support a more effective learning process. Keep spirit, Nezha!'),
	(128, 151, 'Nugi has an excellent understanding of the subjects and is not hesitant to ask questions when in doubt, which is a great quality. However, there are still a few areas that can be improved to help him grow further. He is encouraged to stay focused during lessons and reduce unnecessary movement around the classroom to maintain a better learning environment. Keep up the good work, Nugi!'),
	(129, 152, 'Thara demonstrates an excellent understanding of the lessons and consistently performs well academically. He is socially well-adjusted, gets along with everyone, and is always willing to help and share everything that he has for his classmates. However, he can sometimes get distracted and engage in conversations during lessons. Maintaining focus during class will further enhance his already strong performance. Keep up the good work, Thara!'),
	(130, 153, 'Shasa has a good understanding in all subjects, but she can achieve even better results with increased focus and dedication to her studies. She is encouraged to maintain her active use of English, which is commendable. On the other hand, she should stay more focused during lessons and speak only when necessary to avoid distractions. Keep up the good effort, Shasa!'),
	(131, 154, 'Shavira has demonstrated a good understanding of the material and has shown potential to achieve more. However, developing a stronger sense of competition and a drive to excel will help unlock his full potential and improve overall performance. Stay positive and trust in your abilities, Shavira!'),
	(132, 155, 'Zaura demonstrates a very strong understanding of her lessons, with particularly good performance in certain subjects. She is highly responsible and consistently submits her assignments promptly, often being the fastest in class. However, she is encouraged to expand her social circle beyond her close friends. Building connections with a wider group of classmates will help her develop stronger communication and teamwork skills. Keep up the excellent work, Zaura!'),
	(133, 156, 'Finally Abhinaya has finished his study in the 4th grade. He demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. He needs to pay more attention and more support from the parents during home learning. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Abhinaya will study harder and improve his achievements better.'),
	(134, 157, 'Finally Adriello has finished his study in the 4th grade well. He begins to show good progress in his study. He has improved emotional abilities appropriately. He needs to be more active and more enthusiastic in class activities. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Adriello can be more concerned to his discipline and study.'),
	(135, 158, 'Finally Adzkia Jola has finished her study in the 4th grade. She is always willing to listen to instructions during class activities. She tends to follow the class rules respectfully. She needs to be encouraged to express her feelings and opinions more. Hopefully, in the  5th grade, Adzkia Jola will be more active and confident to share her ideas or confusions with the teachers.  '),
	(136, 159, 'Finally Aeenha has finished her study in the 4th grade well. She demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. She has made very good academic and social progress. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Aeenha  will keep up her achievements.'),
	(137, 160, 'Finally Arjuna has finished his study in the 4th grade. Sometimes he shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time.  He needs to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Arjuna will be more concerned to his discipline and study.'),
	(138, 161, 'Finally Caroline has finished her study in the 4th grade. She has made some progress in her lessons this term. She does and submits all her tasks on time.  However, she needs to focus more on her attention. This will help her to make better progress in her studies. Study harder in the 5th grade, Caroline! '),
	(139, 162, 'Finally Daniyal has finished his study in the 4th grade. He is a good learner. He shows enthusiasm for classroom activities. However, he likes to do all his works in hurry. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Daniyal will do his works more carefully and show more enthusiasm in learning activities.'),
	(140, 163, 'Finally Diandra has finished her study in the 4th grade well. She can understand her lesson fast. She needs to be more active and confident to share her ideas or confusions to the teachers. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Diandra can participate in learning activities more actively.'),
	(141, 164, 'Finally Fredella has finished her study in the 4th grade well. She demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in some of the subjects.  However, she needs to focus more on her attention. This will help her to make better progress in her studies. Study harder in the 5th grade, Fredella!'),
	(142, 165, 'Finally Ghanny has finished his study in the 4th grade well. He is a friendly and cooperative student. He is kind to others. He is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with the other students in the class. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Ghanny will be more concerned to his study.'),
	(143, 166, 'Finally Habiburrahman has finished his study in the 4th grade. He shows enthusiasm for all his activities. However, he likes to do all his works in hurry. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Habiburrahman will do his works more carefully and show more enthusiasm in learning activities.'),
	(144, 167, 'Finally Kaylee has finished  her study in the 4th grade well. She shows enthusiasm for classroom activities. She shows a better ability to completes  her assignments on time. She always behaves with honesty and integrity at all times. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Kaylee will improve  her achievements better and keep spirit.'),
	(145, 168, 'Finally Kenzo has finished his study in the 4th grade well. He demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. He is active and confident to share his ideas or confusions to the teachers. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Kenzo will keep up his achievements.'),
	(146, 169, 'Finally Micello has finished his study in the 4th grade. He demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. He needs to pay more attention and more support from the parents during home learning. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Micello will study harder and improve his achievements better.'),
	(147, 170, 'Finally Naura has finished her study in the 4th grade well. She demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She is active and confident to share her ideas or confusions to the teachers. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Naura will keep up her achievements.\r\n'),
	(148, 171, 'Finally Aurelya has finished her study in the 4th grade. She demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in some of the subjects and responsibility. Sometimes she needs to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Aurelya will be more concerned to her discipline and study.\r\n'),
	(149, 172, 'Finally Quinn has finished her study in the 4th grade. She demonstrates a developing  level of understanding in some of the subjects. She needs to concentrate more during the lesson. She needs to study harder and review the lesson at home.  Hopefully in the 5th grade, Quinn will participate in learning activities more actively.\r\n'),
	(150, 173, 'Finally Radinka Arkan has finished his study in the 4th grade well. He can understand the lessons well. He needs to be more active and confident to share his ideas or confusions to the teachers. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Arkan can participate in learning activities more confidently.\r\n'),
	(151, 174, 'Finally Raditya has finished his study in the 4th grade well. He shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He can understand the lessons well. However, he still needs some extra prompting to be engaged during and to be more active in class activities. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Raditya will be more active and confident to share his ideas or confusions to the teachers.  \r\n'),
	(152, 175, 'Finally Sabyca has finished her study in the 4th grade. She  demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. However, she likes to do all her works in hurry. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Sabyca will do her works more carefully and show more her enthusiasm in learning activities.\r\n'),
	(153, 176, 'Finally Shanela has finished her study in the 4th grade well. She demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. She has made very good academic and social progress. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Shanela will keep up her achievements.'),
	(154, 177, 'Finally Velove has finished her study in the 4th grade well. She has made some good academic and social progress. However, she needs to participate more activley in a learning discussion. Hopefully in the 5th grade, Velove will be more patient, friendly and enthusiastic in the class activities.'),
	(155, 33, 'He is a nice student. He tries to do his best for his school work. He still needs to improve his self confidence to do his school work independently. Staying focus and pay more attention on the lesson will deliver him to a better result. Keep practising and trying. Always, do your best. Abiyan!'),
	(156, 34, 'He can manages his emotions appropriately, He needs to focus on the task at hand and taking more responsibility are the key to have a better score. Keep studying and be better in the next  grade, Al !'),
	(157, 35, 'She is gaining self- confidence in every tasks given by the teachers especially in Science and English. Alula is a very capable student, She just needs to adopt a positive attitude during all lessons. Study hard in the next grade, Alula!'),
	(158, 37, 'He consistently needs reminders to focus on time management. It would benefit from showing a greater desire to contribute ideas in class and needs frequent reminders to be attentive during instructions and lessons. Keep Spirit and be better in the next grade, Razqa!'),
	(159, 36, 'He perseveres when faced with difficulty by asking questions and trying his best. He also can be counted on to be one of the first students to begin working on the task that is given. Beside that he is easy get distracted that makes him sometimes not focus. He just needs to adopt a positive attitude during all lessons. Good luck in the next grade, Athallah Syafiq !'),
	(160, 38, 'He demonstrates a willing and conscientious effort in his daily work. He also needs to listen to directions more attentively during lessons. Keep showing your improvement, Audric!'),
	(161, 39, 'He consistently needs reminders to focus on time management. He needs to focus on the task at hand and taking more responsibility are the key to have a better score. Keep studying and be better in the next grade, Azril !'),
	(162, 40, 'We are glad that ayra started expressing her needs more verbally. Aiyra is building up herself confidence and is now able to perform in front of the class. Keep doing good work, Aiyra in the next grade !'),
	(163, 41, 'He listens attentively to the responses of others. She is faithfully performs classroom tasks and asks for clarification when she needed. Keep a good work, Farrel!'),
	(164, 42, 'He is interested in his own learning, listens attentively, and makes a solid effort to avoid distractions that could interrupt the learning process. Keep a good work, in the next grade, Fathul !'),
	(165, 43, 'She needs to improve on working independently and be sure to ask for assistance only when it is needed and needs frequent reminders to be attentive during instructions and lessons. Keep Spirit and be better in the next grade, Iken!  '),
	(166, 44, 'She shows responsible behavior, works well with a group and shows appreciation for the efforts of classmates. She show good progress in her study. She tries to speak English actively in the class. Keep showing your improvement. Khansa!'),
	(167, 45, 'She is a joy to be guided. She always on time in every task given and she is very eager to learn. She takes a keen interest in all her works, most agreeable and also a very willing student. However, she has tendency to over chat with her peers at the end of this term. She needs to recognize the value of undivided attention. Otherwise, She is maturing herself nicely this year and we hope this continues until next grade. Good luck in the next grade Zaraa!'),
	(168, 46, 'It has been a pleasure to have Ami enthusiasm, and maturity in my class. She is thoughtful, insightful and thorough in written and verbal communication, and has a talent for expressing her ideas clearly. Keep up your wonderful thing’s in the next grade, Ami !'),
	(169, 47, 'She works well in all basic subject. By the end of the term, she performs well and has become very responsible and reliable. She is able to work independently, follow directions accurately and promptly she always manages to get her work done in a timely and effective manner. Keep up the good work, Nindy in the next grade!'),
	(170, 48, 'We are glad that recently Rachel has started expressing her needs and wants more verbally. She starts to communicate more with her classmates and teachers expressively. Rachel has difficult time focusing her attention on Science’s lesson. Keep up the good work, Rachel!'),
	(171, 49, 'She shows responsible behavior, works well with a group and shows appreciation for the efforts of classmates. She show good progress in her study. She tries to speak English actively in the class. Keep showing your improvement. Raina!'),
	(172, 50, 'He is a cheerful boy. He seems happy in every single activity in the class. He makes friends easily with his peers, his social skill grows independently since the beginning of school year. He shows initiative and looks for new ways to get involved. He asks for clarification when needed. Keep showing your improvement in the next grade, Shaka !'),
	(173, 51, 'She is kind, respectful and helpful when interacting with her peers. She demonstrates a good understanding of all lesson concepts studied and communicates with clarity and good justification of reasoning. Keep up your wonderful thing’s in the next grade, Shenka !'),
	(174, 52, 'She enjoys conversation with friends during free periods. She also needs to listen to directions more attentively during lessons. Keep showing your improvement, Shanum!'),
	(175, 53, 'He is a happy child, he smiles often and is really laid back at everything he does. He has an easy -going personality. We are pleased to inform you that he has shown his improvement in following class rules. Congratulations Zain for your best achievement! '),
	(176, 199, 'Adam shows a good progress in some lessons during this semester but he needs frequent reminders to be attentive during instructions and lessons. He needs to be more confident to do presentation in front of the class. Keep spirit to study, Adam!\r\n\r\n'),
	(177, 200, '•	Anandita is a nice student. She is developing her responsibility and study consistency during this semester. She needs to improve in Science and Social Studies lesson. Keep going on, Anandita!'),
	(178, 201, 'Arian is an obedient student. He shows his good consistency and discipline to do all his tasks during this semester. Also he shows good understanding in all lesson concepts. He is able to follow teacher’s instruction well during the learning process. Very good effort, Arian!	'),
	(179, 202, 'Athar is an active student. He shows his responsibility to complete the tasks given. Also he shows good interest in English and Social Studies. However, he.needs to listen the directions more attentively during lessons. Keep up your high spirit, Athar!'),
	(180, 203, 'Bimo is a cheerful student He is developing his motivation to follow the lesson in the class. He needs improvement to be active while joining the class discussion. He also needs encouragement to build up her self understanding concept of Math . Keep trying to be better, Bimo!	'),
	(181, 204, 'Darletta has a nice attitude. She always tries to be a kind student everyday. Her discipline is very good. She consistently does the good effort on her daily assignments and demonstrates her self understanding concept for each lessons given. Well done Darletta!	'),
	(182, 205, 'Deffa has a good understanding her self concept  in every lesson. He also shows his confidence to answer teacher’s question. He has good interest in Math, Science and Social Studies. Keep your spirit, Deffa!'),
	(183, 206, 'Qaireen has shown her good attention in every class activity. She has shown a good progress in her study concept. She needs to be more active while joining the class discussion. Keep up the good work, Qaireen!.'),
	(184, 207, 'Fathiyya shows her activeness during this semester. She shows a good resposibility to do all his tasks. She needs more improvement in understanding Math lesson. Also she needs to build up her confidence during the class activity. Keep on moving to be better, Fatthiya!'),
	(185, 208, 'Hanin shows her mature to learn as her self concept. She is an active participant in discussion class. She consistently does the good effort on her daily assignments and demonstrates her self understanding concept for each lessons given. Keep up the good work,Hanin!'),
	(186, 209, 'Junior is a good student. He can speak English well. He has good self understanding when facing the lesson. He also starts to be strict to the school rules through remind his friends who is breaking the rules. It’s an excellent improvement of his behaviour. Good luck for the next level, Junior!.	'),
	(187, 210, 'Innaya is a nice student. She is good to all friends and polite to the teachers. In academic, even she has good ability to understand the material, she is still shy to explore her potential in the learning process. Therefore, she needs to improve her self-confidence to have a better progress in the next level. Keep up the good work,Innaya!'),
	(188, 211, 'Izzmi is a good student. She needs to improve some things for the better progress in the next level.  She should study hard to achieve academic school standard, she has to learn to have good self understanding in the learning process.Keep on going to be better, Izzmi!'),
	(189, 212, 'Jesslyne is a nice student. She is good to all friends and polite to the teachers. In academic, even she has good ability to understand the material, she is still shy to explore her potential in the learning process. Therefore, she needs to improve her self-confidence to have a better progress in the next level. Keep up the good work, Jesslyne!'),
	(190, 213, 'Kayyisah has a good understanding her self concept  in every lesson. She also shows her confidence to answer teacher’s question. She has good interest in Math, Science and Social Studies. Keep your spirit, Kayyisah!'),
	(191, 214, 'Baim is a cheerful student. He is always excited to come to school for learning in the class and also to meet his friends. He has good progress when learning in the class. He  knows when he  understands or does not understand the lesson.. Keep your spirit, Baim!	'),
	(192, 215, 'Nabila is developing her study responsibility during this semester. She needs more encouragement to understand her self concept in every lesson.  She needs to build up her confidence during the class activity. Keep up your high spirit, Nabila!'),
	(193, 216, 'Nadya shows good understanding in all lesson concepts. She is able to follow teacher’s instruction well during the learning process. She also shows her good consistency and discipline to do all assignments given. Very good effort, Nadya!	'),
	(194, 217, 'Naufal an active learner. He shows his good consistency and discipline to do all his tasks during this semester. He has good understanding in Math concept. Keep up the good work,Naufal!'),
	(195, 218, 'Dimas an enthusiastic learner. He shows good responsibility during this semester. However, he.needs to listen the directions more attentively during lessons. He also needs to improve his understanding in Social Studies lessons. Keep up your high spirit, Dimas!'),
	(196, 12, 'She is gaining self- confidence. She needs to develop a better sense of responsibility to finish her work especially in science. She tries her best to participate in class discussion and when she speaks, she does with confidence. Reviewing the past lesson more at home will help her to get a better result. Good luck, Ailia!'),
	(197, 13, 'He is trying hard and continues to make steady progress in all subjects. He needs to write carefully for him sometimes does mistake when doing the tasks. It is important that he learns to be a good listener and focus more on paying attention.  Keep your focus up!'),
	(198, 14, 'He is a good and cooperative student. He works democratically with peers. He regulary volunteers to assist in classroom activities. He needs to work carefully to avoid careless mistakes in his schoolwork. We need to encourage him to express his suggestion and feeling about something. He responded appropritely when the teachers guided him if he did something wrong. He welcomed leadership roles in group.'),
	(199, 15, 'He shows his willingness to learn. He consistently completes homework assignments. However, he needs to increase speed in finishing his daily work and comprehension in reading. He also needs to relax and focus on doing his schoolwork. He also likes to help his classmates and teachers. Keep up your spirit, Delwyn!'),
	(200, 16, 'She is gaining self- confidence. She needs to develop a better sense of responsibility to finish her work especially in science. She tries her best to participate in class discussion and when she speaks, she does with confidence. Reviewing the past lesson more at home will help her to get a better result. Good luck, Amaya!'),
	(201, 17, 'She shows respect for teachers and peers. She is honest and trustworthy in dealings with others. She is concerned about the feelings of peers. She should concentrate on science, math and English subject in the coming term because she has learning problems. We need to encourage her to take her work much more seriously.'),
	(202, 18, 'She demonstrates a developing level of understanding in some of the subjects. She shows a better ability to completes her assignments on time. Most of the time, she shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Good Luck, Bee!'),
	(203, 19, 'He has a good basic knowledge. He enjoys spending time with his friends during recess. He should try better in retelling events from a story in a sequential manner. He follows directions effectively and works well with classmates. He has a talent for expressing his ideas clearly. The harder you work, the more luck you seem to have!'),
	(204, 20, 'She is happy child. She smiles often and is really laid back everything does. She has an easy- going personality and it is effortless to be around her. It is important that she learns to be attentive while listening to others. She needs teacher\'s guidance to finish her work on time. It is important that she learns to be a good listener and focus more on paying attention.'),
	(205, 21, 'We are glad that he started expressing his needs more verbally. Fawwaz is building up himself confidence and is now able to perform in front of the class. He works well in all basic subject. By the end of the term, he performs well and has become very responsible and reliable. He can work independently, follow directions accurately and promptly he always manages to get his work done in a timely and effective manner. Good Luck in Primary 2!'),
	(206, 22, 'She shows her best effort. She has made good achievement this semester. She stays on task with little supervision. She always looks for ways to be helpful in the classroom. She treats other students with fairness and understanding. You’re on the right track!'),
	(207, 23, 'He shows his willingness to learn. He consistently completes homework assignments. However, he needs to increase speed in finishing his daily work and comprehension in reading. He also needs to relax and focus on doing his schoolwork. He also likes to help his classmates and teachers. Keep up your spirit, Kenzie!'),
	(208, 24, 'She is a calm student. She seems eager to improve. She has shown good progress this term. She starts to be more confident to speak up and ask when she gets confused.  However, she needs a constant encouragement. Never give up and show your best effort, Keinara!'),
	(209, 25, 'She is gaining self- confidence. She needs to develop a better sense of responsibility to finish her work especially in science. She tries her best to participate in class discussion and when she speaks, she does with confidence. Reviewing the past lesson more at home will help her to get a better result. Good luck, Annasya!'),
	(210, 26, 'We are glad that he started expressing his needs more verbally. El is building up himself confidence and is now able to perform in front of the class. He works well in all basic subject. By the end of the term, he performs well and has become very responsible and reliable. He can work independently, follow directions accurately and promptly he always manages to get his work done in a timely and effective manner. Good Luck, El!'),
	(211, 27, 'We are pleased to inform you that he has shown his improvement in following class rules. Sometimes, he likes to distract others. It is important that he learns to be a good listener and focus more on paying attention.  Keep your focus up, Razki!'),
	(212, 28, 'She is a joy to be guided. She is always on time in every task given and she is very eager to learn. She takes a keen interest in all her works, most agreeable and a very willing student. However, she has tendency to over chat with her peers at the end of this term. She needs to recognize the value of undivided attention. Otherwise, She is maturing herself nicely this year and we hope this continues until next grade. What a wonderful work!'),
	(213, 29, 'She is happy child. She smiles often and is really laid back everything does. She has an easy- going personality and it is effortless to be around her. It is important that she learns to be attentive while listening to others. She needs teacher\'s guidance to finish her work on time. It is important that she learn to be a good listener and focus more on paying attention.'),
	(214, 30, 'She is a joy to be guided. She is always on time in every task given and she is very eager to learn. She takes a keen interest in all her works, most agreeable and a very willing student. However, she has tendency to over chat with her peers at the end of this term. She needs to recognize the value of undivided attention. Otherwise, She is maturing herself nicely this year and we hope this continues until next grade. What a wonderful work!'),
	(215, 31, 'She is a joy to be guided. She is always on time in every task given and she is very eager to learn. She takes a keen interest in all her works, most agreeable and a very willing student. However, she has tendency to over chat with her peers at the end of this term. She needs to recognize the value of undivided attention. Otherwise, She is maturing herself nicely this year and we hope this continues until next grade. What a wonderful work!'),
	(216, 32, 'We are pleased to inform you that he has shown his improvement in following class rules. Sometimes, he likes to distract others. It is important that he learns to be a good listener and focus more on paying attention.  Keep your focus up, Rayyan!'),
	(217, 54, 'Bama is a bright and enthusiastic student who shows excellent understanding in all subjects. He enjoys learning and always tries his best. Bama works very well with his classmates and is kind and helpful during group activities. He often takes the lead in group work and shows strong leadership skills for his age. We are very proud of Bama’s positive attitude and great progress this term. well done, bama!'),
	(218, 55, 'Rizy is an enthusiastic and active learner who enjoys participating in classroom activities. His academic skills are steadily developing, and with continued effort and support, he will make even more progress in all subject areas. Rizy shows a special interest in Physical Education and consistently demonstrates energy and enthusiasm during sports activities. He is confident when expressing his ideas and often takes initiative in group work, showing natural leadership qualities. Keep up the great work, Rizy!'),
	(219, 56, 'Alula has shown remarkable academic progress this semester. She grasps new concepts quickly and demonstrates a strong understanding across subjects. Alula is especially enthusiastic during Physical Education lessons, where she actively participates and shows great energy. In class, she is very engaged and confident in expressing her ideas clearly. Her positive attitude and active involvement contribute greatly to the learning environment. Keep up the excellent work, Alula!'),
	(220, 57, 'Ardi has shown good academic performance throughout this term. He participates actively in class discussions and is always eager to try new things. His curiosity drives him to ask thoughtful questions and explore learning topics with great interest. We appreciate his positive attitude and willingness to learn. Keep up the great work, Ardi!'),
	(221, 58, 'Caca is confident in asking questions when she needs help, which shows her curiosity and willingness to learn. Caca is also kind and friendly toward her classmates, creating a positive atmosphere in the classroom. However, she is encouraged to improve her focus during lessons to maximize her learning potential. To support her development, Caca is advised to read regularly at home to strengthen her vocabulary and comprehension skills. With continued effort and support, she will continue to grow in both academics and behavior. Keep a good work caca!'),
	(222, 59, 'Arshaka has shown good progress in his understanding of various subjects throughout Grade 1. He is curious and not afraid to ask questions when something is unclear, which helps him learn more effectively. Arshaka is also a kind and friendly classmate who gets along well with others and contributes to a positive classroom environment. As a suggestion, reading regularly at home will help strengthen his literacy skills and support his overall academic growth. Keep up the great work, Arshaka!'),
	(223, 60, 'Azka has shown good academic development and continues to make steady progress in all subjects. He is highly enthusiastic during drawing activities and demonstrates a strong sense of creativity in his artwork. To support his overall growth, Azka is encouraged to work on time management so he can complete tasks more efficiently during school hours. Keep up the good work, Azka!'),
	(224, 61, 'Clemira has shown excellent academic progress and consistently performs at a high level across all subjects. She displays a strong enthusiasm for learning and is always eager to try new things. Clemira is also very respectful and consistently follows classroom and school r'),
	(225, 62, 'Maryam demonstrates a positive attitude toward her classmates and interacts well with her peers. She completes her tasks on time and shows great discipline in following classroom routines. Maryam is very enthusiastic during drawing activities and displays a high level of creativity in her artwork. Well done, Maryam!'),
	(226, 63, 'Zahra shows strong academic abilities and consistently performs well in her studies. She often expresses original ideas and enjoys exploring different forms of artistic expression, demonstrating creativity and enthusiasm in her work. Well done, Zahra!'),
	(227, 64, 'Isvara has shown great improvement in managing her emotions during challenging situations. She is becoming more confident when participating in group discussions. Isvara is always polite and gets along well with her classmates. She also shows a strong sense of responsibility in completing her school tasks. Well done, Isvara!'),
	(228, 65, 'Kayra is a cheerful and kind student who always shows respect to teachers and friends. She enjoys learning and actively participates in class activities. Kayra works well with others and shows responsibility in completing her school tasks. She continues to grow in confidence and learning. Great job, Kayra!'),
	(229, 66, 'Leiana is a polite and thoughtful student who is able to express her feelings clearly and appropriately. She consistently demonstrates diligence in completing her assignments and submits her work on time. Throughout the school year, Leiana has shown significant progress in her learning and personal development. Well done, Leiana. Keep up the excellent work!'),
	(230, 67, 'Mikaila is a kind and respectful student who approaches her learning with a positive attitude. She enjoys participating in class activities and works well with her peers. Mikaila completes her assignments with care and continues to make steady progress in her learning. Well done, Mikaila!'),
	(231, 68, 'Ghani is an active and enthusiastic student who enjoys participating in class activities. He often shares creative and thoughtful ideas, which contribute positively to group discussions. Ghani shows great curiosity and enthusiasm in his learning. Keep up the great work, Ghani!'),
	(232, 69, 'Nayara is a quiet and shy student who has started to engage more with her classmates and is now willing to speak in class. She has shown good progress in her social development and is becoming more comfortable in group settings. There is still room for improvement in her academic performance, and with continued support and effort, she will continue to grow. Keep going, Nayara!'),
	(233, 70, 'Aini is a kind and caring student who shows genuine concern for her classmates. She is always willing to help others and contributes to creating a positive and supportive classroom environment. Well done, Aini!'),
	(234, 71, 'Rafandara is a diligent and cooperative student who works well with both his peers and teachers. He demonstrates positive behavior and emotional maturity, showing respect and kindness in various situations. Rafandara also has a notable talent in art and craft, where his creativity truly shines. With continued effort and a positive attitude, he has great potential to further improve his achievements. Keep up the excellent work!'),
	(235, 72, 'Mahrez is a friendly and enthusiastic student who brings positive energy to the classroom. He participates actively in class and interacts well with his classmates. Mahrez shows good academic progress and demonstrates a clear understanding of the concepts taught. With his consistent effort and positive attitude, he continues to grow both academically and socially. Excellent work, Mahrez!'),
	(236, 73, 'Rafi is a cheerful and respectful student who participates well in class activities. He is able to get along with his classmates and shows a positive attitude towards learning. With continued effort, Rafi has the potential to make steady progress in both his academic and personal growth. Keep it up, Rafi!'),
	(237, 74, 'Zunaira is a kind and respectful student who shows a positive attitude toward learning. She gets along well with her classmates and participates actively in class activities. Zunaira has shown good academic progress and completes her tasks with care and responsibility. Keep up the great work, Zunaira!'),
	(238, 178, 'Kemal demonstrates a good level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. He demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. He is able to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Good job, Kemal!'),
	(239, 179, 'Abraham demonstrates a good level of understanding in most of the subjects. He shows a better ability to complete his assignments on time. He demonstrates a good level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. He is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Abraham shows good enthusiasm on the lesson this term. Keep motivated, Abraham!'),
	(240, 180, 'Adeeva demonstrates a well developing level of understanding in some of the subjects. She seldom completes her assignments on time. She demonstrates a developing level of responsibility and sometimes she forgets to bring her books and classroom tasks. She needs to learn how to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. You can do better, Adeeva!'),
	(241, 181, 'Nuraffa demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in some of the subjects. He seldom completes his assignments on time. Nuraffa demonstrates a beginning level of behaviour with honesty and integrity at all times. He makes friends quickly in the classroom and chooses to spend free time with friends. Nuraffa needs to show more enthuasism on lesson in class. Let’s improve your skill, Nuraffa!'),
	(242, 182, 'Letta demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in some of the subjects. She seldom completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Letta show her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Sometimes, she forgets to bring her books and classroom tasks. So, Letta needs to be more responsible in preparing her school bag. Keep trying your best, Letta!'),
	(243, 183, 'Khanza demonstrates an excellent level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. She demonstrates a very well level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. She is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. You are smart and capable, Khanza!'),
	(244, 184, 'Alisha demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. She seldom completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Alisha show her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Alisha needs to show interest and enthuasiasm on lesson. I believe you can do better, Alisha!'),
	(245, 185, 'Asheela demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Most of the time, Asheela shows her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is gaining confidence to make friends in the classroom, but sometimes chooses to spend free time alone. Asheela needs to bring food and eat with her friends in class. You should know that you have bright personality, Asheela!'),
	(246, 186, 'Naila demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. She seldom completes her assignments on time. Rarely does Naila show her enthusiasm during the lesson time. She is able to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Naila needs to focus more in learning process in class and should learn more at home. You have a great potential, Naila!'),
	(247, 187, 'Brava demonstrates a good level of understanding in most of the subjects. He shows a better ability to complete his assignments on time. Rarely does Brava show his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He makes friends quickly in the classroom and chooses to spend free time with friends. Brava needs to manage his time in playing soccer, so he will not be tired in learning process. You are getting better every day, Brava!'),
	(248, 188, 'Calyla demonstrates an excellent level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Calyla shows progress in behaving with honesty and integrity at all times. She needs to learn how to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Calyla needs to be more independent in taking care of herself especially in carrying school supplies. You are capable of amazing things, Calyla!'),
	(249, 189, 'Atha demonstrates a good level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. He demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. He makes friends quickly in the classroom and chooses to spend free time with friends. Atha needs to be more active in class. Don’t be afraid to make mistakes, Atha!'),
	(250, 190, 'Karin demonstrates an excellent level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. She demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. She makes friends quickly in the classroom and chooses to spend free time with friends. Karin just needs to be more cheerful and show her feelings to her classmates. Believe in yourself, Karin!'),
	(251, 191, 'Zavierre demonstrates a good level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. Some of the time, Zavierre shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He needs to learn how to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Zavierre needs to be more on time to come to school. Keep trying, Zavierre!'),
	(252, 192, 'Nayyara demonstrates a developing level of understanding in most of the subjects. She shows a better ability to complete her assignments on time. Nayyara shows progress in behaving with honesty and integrity at all times. She is able to get better score in many subjects if she focus more on lessons. I believe You can do it, Nayyara!'),
	(253, 193, 'Rafandra demonstrates an excellent level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. Most of the time, Rafandra shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He is able to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Rafandra did a good job inside and outside class. He can do many things at the same time. Your hardwork is paying off, Rafandra!'),
	(254, 194, 'Raiden demonstrates a good level of understanding in most of the subjects. He shows a better ability to complete his assignments on time. Rarely does Raiden show his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He needs to learn how to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Raiden needs to manage his emotion and strengthen when communicating with his friends. I believe in you, Raiden!'),
	(255, 195, 'Angel demonstrates a very good level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. She demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. She is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Angel needs to be more confident to show her talents and be more active in class. You are capable of many amazing things, Angel!'),
	(256, 196, 'Shailene demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. She demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. She makes friends quickly in the classroom and chooses to spend free time with friends. Shailene needs to show off her good speaking ability in class. You have just about to master it!'),
	(257, 197, 'Sofia demonstrates a well-developed level of understanding in most of the subjects. She always completes her assignments on time. Sofia always behaves with honesty and integrity at all times. She is able to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Sofia needs to focus more in on lesson. She treats other students with fairness and understanding. Keep up the great work, Sofia!'),
	(258, 198, 'Ukasyah demonstrates a developing level of understanding in most of the subjects. He always completes his assignments on time. He is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Ukasyah needs to show his antuasism on lessons to get the better result. He is respectful of other students and teachers. You are making progress, Ukasyah!');
INSERT INTO `nilaideskripsimid` (`id`, `siswa_kelas_id`, `deskripsi`) VALUES
	(24, 12, 'Ailia is improving her ability to pay attention to directions. She is a very hard worker and has excellent vocabulary skills for her age. She enjoys reading and writing in English lesson. She is making progress in all academic areas. She sometimes rushes through assignments and makes careless mistakes. All the practicing she does at home and the encouragement she gets will help her in class.'),
	(25, 13, 'Alex is a nice student in the morning. On the other hand, he needs to be reminded by the teacher to finish his schoolwork. He must continue to improve his work habits, as we mentioned in earlier meetings. We need to encourage him to take his work much more seriously. Moreover, he needs to be more focused when the teacher explains the materials.'),
	(26, 14, 'Alif is an excellent public speaker. He regularly volunteers to assist in classroom activities. He needs to have encouraged himself to take his work much more seriously. However, he makes friends quickly in all grades. He enjoys conversation with friends during free periods.'),
	(27, 15, 'Delwyn remains focused on the activity at hand, for example art and craft activity. He does not give up when facing a task that is difficult and always does his best. He is always enthusiastic when completing his work. He is smiling a lot.  He is kind and helpful to everyone in the classroom. He treated school property and the belongings of others with care and respect. He sometimes needed guidance to finish his schoolwork.'),
	(28, 16, 'Amaya is committed to doing her best. She responds appropriately when corrected. She is honest and trustworthy in dealings with others. She also displays good citizenship by assisting other students. She perseveres when faced with difficulty by asking questions and trying her best. She is kind, respectful dan helpful when interacting with her peers.'),
	(29, 136, 'Abi has shown good academic ability throughout the year. However, there has been a slight decline in performance this term. He tends to get distracted easily, which affects his ability to engage actively in class discussions and group work. Believe in yourself, Abi!'),
	(30, 75, 'Arshaka demonstrates a developing level of understanding in some of the subjects. He shows a better ability to complete his assignments on time. He demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. He is gaining confidence to cooperate and work well with any of the other students in the class. Nice going!'),
	(31, 219, 'Affandy demonstrates a beginning level of understanding in most of the subjects. He seldom completes his assignments on time. Some of the time, Affandy shows his enthusiasm during the lesson time. He is always encouraged to make friends in the classroom and most of the time chooses to spend free time alone. Keep moving, you are improving!'),
	(32, 96, 'Ayesha continues to do well in this semester. She is a friendly and she is able to initiate conversation and play with her classmates. Academically, Ayesha needs more review in understanding all the subjects. I do believe she has great potential, and she only needs to be more confident for that. In math she is able to route count multiplication, she needs more practice to read. I hope that support from the parents and keep practicing regularly at home could bring her back on track. Well done, Ayesha! I can’t wait to see that you would catch up on the next lesson. '),
	(33, 240, 'Dhafin is a calm and reliable student who has shown noticeable improvement across most subjects this year. His friendly nature makes him well-liked by peers, and he consistently shows responsibility in group work. To continue growing, Dhafin is encouraged to build more confidence in expressing his ideas, both in class discussions and during presentations. You’ve made great progress, Dhafin — trust in yourself and let your voice be heard!'),
	(34, 241, 'Keyla brings joyful energy to the classroom and is loved by her classmates for her cheerful spirit and kindness. Her improvement in academic performance this year has been truly remarkable, a testament to her hard work and dedication. To help her learning even more, Keyla is encouraged to find moments of calm and focus during class activities. Keep shining, Keyla — your energy is a gift, and when balanced with focus, it will take you far!'),
	(35, 242, 'Azeera is a polite and thoughtful student who follows class rules diligently. Her storytelling ability adds a unique charm to her character. She has shown good progress in attendance and punctuality, and always tries to complete the tasks given. To continue progressing, Azeera is encouraged to develop more independence and motivation in her studies. Keep trying, Azeera — you have a gentle strength that will grow with each new challenge you face!'),
	(36, 243, 'Shanum is a talented and intelligent student who consistently excels in her academic subjects. Her leadership qualities shine in both class and extracurricular activities. She is resilient, loyal, and sets a great example for her peers. To reach even greater heights, Shanum is encouraged to work on accuracy when answering test questions. You’re truly a star, Shanum — your talents and determination are sure to lead you to great success!'),
	(37, 244, 'Cantika is a cheerful and polite student who brightens the classroom with her melodious singing and friendly attitude. She has shown significant improvement in her academic performance and is capable of completing tasks well. To continue growing, Cantika should focus on improving her concentration during lessons. Keep singing your way through learning, Cantika — your voice and positivity are your strengths!'),
	(38, 245, 'Felice is a highly intelligent and caring student who always brings empathy and optimism into the classroom. Her ability to focus, paired with her curiosity and strong knowledge base, make her a standout learner. Felice’s consistent motivation and joy in learning inspire those around her. Keep soaring, Felice — your heart and mind make a powerful combination!'),
	(39, 246, 'Dastan is a thoughtful and curious student with a natural talent for analysis. His class participation has improved notably, and he approaches learning with an open and empathic mindset. To improve further, Dastan should focus on sharpening his listening skills and following instructions more attentively. Keep asking questions and exploring, Dastan — your thoughtful nature will guide your growth!'),
	(40, 247, 'Rose brings creativity and positivity to everything she does. Her sense of humor and proactive attitude make her a joy to have in class. To unlock her full potential, Rose is encouraged to put more effort into studying and reviewing class material consistently. Your bright spirit is contagious, Rose — stay determined, and success will follow!'),
	(41, 248, 'Hilal is a calm and optimistic student who shows great empathy toward others. He has a quiet perseverance and is beginning to show more determination in his work. With continued effort, especially when tasks become more challenging, Hilal can achieve even greater results. Stay strong and keep trying, Hilal — your kindness and patience are true strengths!'),
	(42, 249, 'Jasmine is a hardworking and insightful student who consistently demonstrates motivation and attentiveness in class. Her thoughtful contributions and friendly demeanor make her a wonderful peer and learner. Jasmine’s dedication to her studies will serve her well in the years to come. Keep up the excellent work, Jasmine — your perseverance and insight are truly admirable!'),
	(43, 250, 'Revaldi is a determined and collaborative student who works well with peers. He takes on tasks with a positive attitude and shows steady progress in his work. To reach his full potential, Revaldi is encouraged to stay consistent in completing his daily responsibilities without reminders. You’re on the right path, Revaldi — with continued focus, you’ll achieve great things!'),
	(44, 251, 'Radhitya is a motivated and organized student who approaches his studies with determination and a positive mindset. He is friendly, patient, and contributes positively to group activities. His consistent effort and dedication to learning are commendable. Keep striving, Radhitya — your strong character and discipline will lead you to success!'),
	(45, 252, 'Rezki is a creative and energetic student who enjoys sports and interacting with others. He brings enthusiasm to all activities, but sometimes struggles to manage emotions and maintain concentration in class. With continued support in emotional regulation and focus, Rezki can make great strides. Stay balanced, Rezki — your energy is a strength when guided with purpose!'),
	(46, 253, 'Shanon is an analytical and enthusiastic learner who approaches tasks with curiosity and care. She is well-organized and always attentive, making her a reliable contributor in class discussions. Her love for learning is clear and will serve her well in the future. Keep exploring, Shanon — your enthusiasm and intellect will take you far!'),
	(47, 254, 'Vino is an enthusiastic and motivated student who brings a lively spirit to the classroom. His positive attitude toward learning is commendable. To continue progressing, Vino should work on improving his focus during lessons to fully absorb the material. Keep up the great effort, Vino — your enthusiasm is powerful when paired with focus!'),
	(48, 97, 'Kenzie is a loveable boy and diligent student, he is always very enthusiast and tries his best to participate in all activities in school. Kenzie is a friendly boy who likes to play and to have conversation with his friends. Academically, Kenzie has no difficulties in lesson. He can complete all the tasks given independently. I am proud for all the great improvements you have made. Good Job, Kenzie! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(49, 98, 'Alifa has made a very nice progress in this semester. She begins to become an active participant during the lesson and class discussion. She follows and listens to the instruction given by the teachers attentively. Academically, She demonstrates a well-developed level of responsibility and doesn’t need to be consistently reminded of how to perform daily classroom tasks. She is beginning to be confident to make friends in the classroom. Good work'),
	(50, 99, 'Alma continues to be awesome. She is beginning to be more independent and shows confidence in completing all the tasks given by the teacher. Alma enjoys spending time with her friends, loves to play and able to initiate conversation and play with her friends .Academically, Alma need more review in science, she is able to understand multiplication. I am proud for all improvements you have made. Good Job Alma! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(51, 100, 'Ar Rayyan has made a steady progress. He becomes attentive during lessons and follows the instructions given. He has been consistently progressing in all academic area. Ar Rayyan is a friendly boy who likes to initiate conversation and play with his friends. Ar Rayyan is doing well but I know he can do even better! In language area Ar Rayyan still need confidence to speak in English and In Math Ar Rayyan is fluent in rote multiplication. Ar Rayyan only needs more practice in Science. I do believe with a lot of practice at home he could improve his skills. Good Job, Ar Rayyan!'),
	(52, 101, 'Arsyila is  a sweet student, she is always very enthusiast and tries her best to participate in all the activities in school. Arsyila is a friendly girl who likes to initiate conversation and play with her friends. Academically, Arsyila has no difficulties in English especially in dictation. In math Arsyila still need more practice in multiplication. She can complete all the tasks given independently. I am proud for all the great improvements you have made. Good Job, Arsyila! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(53, 102, 'Asyifa is a sweet student, she is always very enthusiast and tries her best to participate in all the activities in school. Asyifa is a friendly girl who likes to initiate conversation and play with her friends. Academically, Asyifa has no difficulties in math especially in multiplication. She can complete all the tasks given independently. I am proud for all the great improvements you have made. Good Job, Asyifa! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(54, 103, 'Azka is a sweet boy and diligent student, he is always very enthusiast and tries his best to participate in all the activities in school. Azka is a friendly boy who likes to initiate to play and to have conversation with his friends. Academically, Azka has no difficulties in lesson. He can complete all the tasks given independently. I am proud for all the great improvements you have made. Good Job, Azka! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(55, 104, 'Halumi is sweet student, she is always very enthusiast and tries her best to participate in all activities in school. Halumi is a friendly girl who likes to initiate conversation and play with her friends. Academically, Halumi has no difficulties in math especially in multiplication. She can complete all the tasks given independently. I am proud for all the great improvements you have made. Good Job, Halumi! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing'),
	(56, 105, 'Keenan continues to be awesome. He is beginning to be more independent and shows confidence in completing all the tasks given by the teacher. Keenan enjoys spending time with his friends, loves to play and be able to initiate conversation and play with his friends. Academically Keenan is able to understand math to route count multiplication. I am proud for all improvements you have made. Good Job Keenan! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(57, 106, 'Mazel has made a very good progress this semester. He shows an excellent attitude toward learning. He works hard to complete his assignments independently and in a timely manner. Academically. In math Mazel need more practice in multiplication. Mazel is able to initiate conversation and play with his classmates. He begins to share and play together with his friends. Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing. Well done Mazel!'),
	(58, 107, 'Rifqi has made a steady progress in this term. He becomes attentive during lessons and follows the instructions given. He has been consistently progressing in all academic areas. Rifqi is a friendly boy who likes to initiate conversation and play with his friends. Rifqi is doing well but I know he can do even better! In language, Rifqi need more practice and review multiplication. I do believe with a lot of practice at home he could improve his language and writing skills. Good Job, Rifqi!'),
	(59, 108, 'Rabbani has continuously done well in the class. He is a friendly boy who like to initiate conversation and play with his classmates. He can play nicely with his friends. In class, we often remind Rabbani to speak in English with his friends. Academically, Rabbani needs more practice and review multiplication. I do believe with both support from parents and teachers could help him to improve his skills. Good Job, Rabbani Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(60, 109, 'Nayyara is a lovable girl, who likes to share food and play nicely with her classmates. During the lesson she is an active participant who enjoys singing and dancing. Academically, Nayyara has no difficulties in multiplication. She is also able to speak English fluently. She is able to follow the teacher’s instructions and complete the tasks given. Good Job Nayyara! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.\r\n'),
	(61, 110, 'Niki has made a very good progress this semester. He shows an excellent attitude toward learning. He works hard to complete his assignments independently and in a timely manner. Academically, In math Niki need more practice in multiplication. Niki is able to initiate conversation and play with his classmates. He begins to share and play together with his friends. Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing. Well done Niki!'),
	(62, 111, 'Prabu continues to be awesome in this semester. He works hard to complete his assignments in a timely manner. He is a friendly boy who likes to play nicely and share his toys with his friends. Academically, Prabu has difficulties in English. In math Prabu still need more practice in multiplication, he needs more practice in reading correctly. Although there has been some improvement, he still needs to review them on daily basis in order to strengthen the skills. Keep doing all the great things you are doing, Prabu! '),
	(63, 112, 'Raihan has continuously done well in the class. He is a friendly boy who likes to initiate conversation and play with his classmates. He can play nicely with his friends. In class, we often remind Raihan to speak in English with his friends. Academically, Raihan is able to route count multiplication. I do believe with both support from parents and teachers it could help him to improve his skills. Good Job, Raihan Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(64, 113, 'Runako continues to be awesome. He is beginning to be more independent and shows confident in completing all the tasks given by the teacher. Runako enjoys spending time with his friends, loves to play and be able to initiate conversation and play with his friends. He sings and dances confidently in the class. Academically Runako is able to understand math to route count multiplication. I am proud for all improvements you have made. Good Job Runako! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(65, 95, 'Sabila is a lovable girl who likes to share food and play nicely with her classmates. During the lesson she is an active participant who enjoys drawing. Academically, Sabila has no difficulties in multiplication. She is also able to speake English fluently. She is able to follow the teacher’s instructions and complete the tasks given. Good Job Sabila! Keep up all the wonderful things you are doing.'),
	(66, 115, 'Zachary has made a steady progress in this term. He becomes attentive during lessons and follows the instructions given. He has been consistently progressing in all academic areas. Zachary is a friendly boy who likes to initiate conversation and play with his friends. Zachary is doing well but I know he can do even better! In language, Zachary need more practice and review on multiplication. I do believe with a lot of practice at home it could improve his language and writing skills. Good Job, Zachary!'),
	(67, 156, 'Abhinaya is a good student. He begins to show good progress in his study. However, he needs to pay more attention and be more active in learning activities. Reviewing and remembering what had been taught is needed for him to improve his academic performance. Study harder, Abhinaya!'),
